  "distinctions": [
    "Illustrated animal scenes are defined by the depicted action and substantive props, not merely the animal name. A reading frog on a lily pad, a puffin knitting, and an owl climbing a book ladder are different visual compositions.",
    "Garment construction activities retain their physical purpose and geometry: grading layered seam widths, understitching a facing, transferring point marks, and clipping a curved allowance are not split by incidental textile changes.",
    "Functional mechanisms with distinct operations remain separate: a spring purse frame, a rotating turnlock, and a roll-top closure are not treated as the same motif merely because all close a bag.",
    "No repeated styling family based on warm layers, a garment draped over a chair, or displaying a garment lining was authored. Interior sewing views describe construction operations rather than a lining-reveal styling family."
  ],
